I am analysing a multi-season occupancy data set that has a treatment
applied to ~50% of sites each year. It is the same treatment each year to the
same sets of sites, but I am interested in finding whether the treatment has
the same or different effect each season.

I have coded the YearlySiteCovs of Treatment with a
combination of treatment and year, e.g. “Y17”, “N17”, “Y18”, “N18”,”Y19”,”N19”
for yes/no treatment in 2017, 2018 and 2019. When analysing using colext with Treatment
as a factor in gamma and/or epsilon formulas it successfully runs, but the summary
output compares each level of the Treatment factor to the base/intercept value, which by default is
the first listed alphabetically “N17”. This default can be changed by setting levels()
of the factor and reordering so the required base level is first, but still does not allow me to specify pairwise comparisons within years, such as “N18” vs “Y18”.

When using LM/GLM/GLMM etc you can set the contrasts for levels
of a factor manually, and it is also possible to set these in the unmarkedMultFrame
for the factor. E.g.:

contrasts(umf@yearlySiteCovs$Treatment) <- my.contrasts

but this does not appear to affect the model in any way.

1)
Is there a way to manually specify contrasts for
factors in a colext (or occu) model, or have I asked too much of the package?

2)
Given I can manually set the levels() of the
factor, I could conceivably change the base level and re-run the model several
times to receive the individual a priori pairwise contrasts I am interested in. Would
this be a useable workaround or am I breaking other assumptions with this approach?

Many thanks,

Alistair

