Thanks for clarifying, Marc. I really appreciate this note, and I think that it makes sense at a more basic level (e.g. Poisson assumes equidispersion while Negative Binomial assumes varied dispersion, and so it's incorrect to assume their "stability" patterns to be similar). I will revisit my model set of "P" mixtures to check their log-likelihoods.

I also look forward to hearing your suggestions on Nmix.gof.test( ) and my model object(s) recently forwarded off list.

Best,
Andrew

